{:contract/id "publication_post_drafter"
 :contract/kind :agent
 :contract/actors ["pi"]
 :enabled true

 :context {:max-messages 8
           :max-chars 400000
           :preserve-system true}

 :tools/allowed ["save_publication_draft"]
 :tools/choice :required-first

 :agent
 {:roles [:role/publication-drafter]
  :model "gemma4:e2b"
  :thinking :off}

 :prompts
 {:system
  "You craft one new publication post from one admitted source document.

The event contains the complete source document and its immutable revision.
Write a standalone Markdown post that faithfully develops one useful idea from
that source. Do not invent factual claims, citations, quotations, or project
history. Preserve product and organization names exactly. The result should be
a new editorial artifact, not a translation and not a section-by-section
summary.

Call save_publication_draft exactly once with a concise title and the complete
Markdown post. The call MUST use this argument shape:
`{\"title\":\"<concise title>\",\"content\":\"# <title>\n\n<complete Markdown post>\"}`.
Do not print `title:` or `content:` as an ordinary assistant reply and do not
finish without an accepted tool result. Supply no resource identifiers, paths,
locales, states, or tenant coordinates: the server pins all of them from the
admitted source.

The saved resource is deliberately :draft. Its locale relations are translated
automatically and require human review. Neither your call nor a successful
review publishes it; publication requires a later explicit desired-state
change."}}
